<!-- DETECTION TESTING -->
<section class="vx-section" aria-labelledby="proven-title">
  <div class="vx-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Detection Testing</div>
    <h2 id="proven-title">Reconstructed attacks in the test suite</h2>
    <p>The regression suite rebuilds known supply chain compromises from their public write-ups and checks that vexes flags each one. These are fixtures written after the fact, so passing them shows the signals fire on patterns already understood — not that vexes would have caught the original attack, or will catch the next one.</p>
    <div class="vx-table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Reconstructed attack detection">
      <table class="vx-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Attack</th>
            <th scope="col">Year</th>
            <th scope="col">Technique</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>axios RAT</td><td>2026</td><td>Hijacked maintainer, hidden RAT dropper</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Shai-Hulud worm</td><td>2025</td><td>Self-replicating via chalk/debug</td></tr>
          <tr><td>event-stream</td><td>2018</td><td>Social engineering, encrypted bitcoin payload</td></tr>
          <tr><td>ua-parser-js</td><td>2021</td><td>Account hijack, cryptominer + stealer</td></tr>
          <tr><td>litellm/TeamPCP</td><td>2026</td><td>CI/CD compromise, K8s lateral movement</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Typosquatting</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>expresss, loadash, reqeusts name confusion</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Synthetic fixtures</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>WASM payloads, DNS exfil, capability escalation</td></tr>
