<!-- FEATURES -->
<section class="vx-section" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="vx-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Features</div>
    <h2 id="features-title">What else is in the box</h2>
    <div class="vx-features-grid" role="list">
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>AI-Assisted Triage &mdash; Opt-In</h3>
        <p><code>vexes explain</code> groups findings and suggests an order to work through them, in plain English. Off unless you set your own <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code>. Only finding summaries are sent; source code is not. Like any model output, check it before acting on it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>SARIF for Code Scanning</h3>
        <p>SARIF 2.1.0 output with cross-run fingerprints. <code>--format sarif</code> uploads to GitHub code scanning. The Action reports findings by default and fails the build only when you ask it to.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Pre-Install Guard</h3>
        <p>Wraps <code>npm install</code> and analyzes new packages before install scripts run. Diffs the lockfile, stops on critical signals, prompts on high ones, then hands off to the real install. It only sees what the analysis layers see.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Checked Fix Recommendations</h3>
        <p>Suggested upgrade versions are looked up in OSV first, so the recommendation isn't a version with its own known advisory. That check is only as current as OSV.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>CI/CD Integration</h3>
        <p>GitHub Actions annotations, SARIF output for Advanced Security, and watch mode for continuous lockfile monitoring.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Fail Loud, Not Clean</h3>
        <p>If queries fail, vexes exits with code 2 and prints SCAN INCOMPLETE. A failed scan should not look like a clean one.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>No Runtime Dependencies</h3>
        <p>A scanner's own dependency chain is attack surface, so vexes ships without one. The acorn parser is vendored into the source tree. SQLite comes from Node.js.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vx-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Signals Config Can't Silence</h3>
        <p><code>KNOWN_COMPROMISED</code>, <code>PHANTOM_DEPENDENCY</code>, <code>CIRCULAR_STAGING</code>, and <code>CAPABILITY_ESCALATION</code> stay on. A checked-in config file cannot suppress them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

