<!-- SECURITY -->
<section class="vx-section" aria-labelledby="security-title">
  <div class="vx-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Security Design</div>
    <h2 id="security-title">Handling untrusted input</h2>
    <p>vexes reads code and metadata it has no reason to trust. These are the measures in place for that. There has been no external security audit.</p>
    <ul class="vx-security-list" role="list">
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>No runtime dependencies</strong> — a scanner's own dependency chain is attack surface. Acorn is vendored. SQLite is a Node.js built-in.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>Terminal escape stripping</strong> — package-supplied text is filtered before printing. CSI sequences, OSC (BEL and ST), DCS/APC/PM/SOS, C1 control codes, and bare ESC bytes are removed.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>No shell in the guard path</strong> — guard uses <code>execFileSync</code> with no shell and an allowlist of known package managers. Fix commands are shell-escaped before display.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>Download limits</strong> — tarball downloads enforce streaming size limits, HTTPS-only URLs, and a registry host allowlist.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>Fix versions checked first</strong> — suggested versions are looked up in OSV before they are shown, so a recommendation isn't a version with its own known advisory.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="vx-security-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span class="vx-security-text"><strong>Prototype pollution protection</strong> — config file merging rejects <code>__proto__</code>, <code>constructor</code>, and <code>prototype</code> keys.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
